/// mlrepro — Type.of does NOT ground a function stored as a MAP VALUE: two maps whose values are functions
/// with DIFFERENT domains reflect the SAME type, so Type.eq wrongly returns `true`. (corpus-hardening,
/// 2026-07-16, found by v-iterators for corpus-bugfix's Type.of/Type.eq reflection cluster)
///
/// This is the MAP-VALUE facet of the function-domain reflection leak family that v-inference has been
/// closing position-by-position: the tuple/list/record-element facet and the SUM-VARIANT-payload facet are
/// fixed + pinned (07-type-system.sexp "Type.of grounds a function stored inside a compound value's element"
/// / "… inside a SUM VARIANT payload"). The MAP-VALUE position was NOT covered and is STILL BUGGY: a
/// function stored as a `Map` value has its domain left `Any` in the reflected type, so two maps holding
/// `Int64 -> Int64` vs `Bool -> Int64` value-functions reflect the same `(Map Int64 (-> Any Int64))` and
/// `Type.eq` folds to a wrong `true`.
///
/// OWNER: v-inference (owns `reflected_ty` / the domain-grounding recursion). Fix direction = the same as
/// the sum-payload facet: when reflecting a `Map` value type, recurse into the VALUE type and ground a
/// function value from its body (re-run the relevant scheme with the grounded value type), instead of
/// taking the bottom-up `(-> Any R)`. The KEY position is likely also worth checking (a fn key is unusual
/// but Map keys must be ordered, so probably N/A — value is the real gap).
///
/// CHECK vs LOWER: `cdz check` PASSES (exit 0) — the wrong `true` is a compile-time FOLD of Type.eq over the
/// under-grounded reflected types, so it is an inference/reflection bug, not a lowering one.
///
/// EXPECTED (when fixed): `map-value fn domains differ` → Type.eq FALSE (distinct types); the SAME-domain
/// control already reflects equal. Becomes a graded pass then (corpus-bugfix will promote).

def f(x) = x + 1
def g(b) = if b then 0 else 1

/// BUG: distinct value-fn domains (Int64->Int64 vs Bool->Int64) must reflect DIFFERENT map types → Type.eq
/// false. Currently returns a wrong `true` (the trap fires).
@test
def map-value-fn-domains-differ() =
  if Type.eq(Type.of(Map.insert(Map.empty, 1, f)), Type.of(Map.insert(Map.empty, 1, g)))
  then trap("BUG: Int64->Int64 map-value fn reflected == Bool->Int64 map-value fn")
  else unit

/// CONTROL (already correct): same value-fn reflects equal.
@test
def map-value-fn-same-is-equal() =
  if Type.eq(Type.of(Map.insert(Map.empty, 1, f)), Type.of(Map.insert(Map.empty, 1, f)))
  then unit else trap("same map-value fn should reflect equal")

/// CONTROL (already correct): non-fn map values distinguish by value type.
@test
def map-nonfn-values-distinguish() =
  if Type.eq(Type.of(Map.insert(Map.empty, 1, 5)), Type.of(Map.insert(Map.empty, 1, true)))
  then trap("map<Int,Int> should differ from map<Int,Bool>") else unit
